  "preamble": "Debuccalization of the coda tap [ɾ] to the glottal fricative [h], losing the oral articulation. Caribbean Spanish aspirates preconsonantal /ɾ/, Western Andalusian Spanish aspirates it before /x/ (realized [h]), and in much of Brazil the coda rhotic is pronounced [h] where European Portuguese keeps the tap [ɾ].",
  "phoneticEffects": "Debuccalization, Lenition",
